WEBVTT

00:00:09,170 --> 00:00:15,450
I have been out of six week break from chemo because of terrible neuropathy from the chemo.

00:00:15,450 --> 00:00:23,810
In the last six weeks, my uncle had phosphatase, a shot up to 268 by ALT to 361 by AST to

00:00:23,810 --> 00:00:24,810
1951.

00:00:24,810 --> 00:00:28,410
Six weeks ago, they were normal or dear normal.

00:00:28,410 --> 00:00:32,210
The only change I made during this time was to start taking SEACT.

00:00:32,210 --> 00:00:37,290
Do you think the SEACT would be causing this increase?

00:00:37,290 --> 00:00:44,730
My ecologist thinks it's the cancer, but he does not know about me taking the SEACT.

00:00:44,730 --> 00:00:45,730
Anything is possible.

00:00:45,730 --> 00:00:54,530
So if you have elevation of alkaline phosphatase, but you don't have elevation of ALT and AST,

00:00:54,530 --> 00:01:01,050
then you don't think that it's still possible, but it's a little lesser degree chance that

00:01:01,050 --> 00:01:04,290
it's something going on at the liver itself.

00:01:04,290 --> 00:01:06,770
You start thinking of tissue damage elsewhere.

00:01:06,770 --> 00:01:12,450
So if you have a known cancer, you look at if my alkaline phosphatase is elevated by

00:01:12,450 --> 00:01:22,050
ALT and AST is spared, then you think that it's the most common thing you would see.

00:01:22,050 --> 00:01:28,130
If you have ALT elevated, AST elevated, like this question along with alkaline phosphatase,

00:01:28,130 --> 00:01:34,250
then you think the irritation or the problem is in the liver itself.

00:01:34,250 --> 00:01:42,530
So I would say that yes, it's possibly the SEACT could be something in that herb combination

00:01:42,530 --> 00:01:44,890
that your liver just doesn't like.

00:01:44,890 --> 00:01:48,930
I would for sure test that by just going off of that.

00:01:48,930 --> 00:01:50,290
Could it be the cancer?

00:01:50,290 --> 00:01:57,130
Well, if it is the cancer, it would be more likely that the cancer is metastasis to the liver

00:01:57,130 --> 00:02:03,810
than it is because the cancer is growing in the breast or growing in the lung or growing

00:02:03,810 --> 00:02:11,130
in the intestinal tract or even metastasized to bone because typically, if you have cancer

00:02:11,130 --> 00:02:16,730
growing in any of those things I just mentioned or metastasized to bone, it wouldn't increase

00:02:16,730 --> 00:02:20,050
ALT and AST.

00:02:20,050 --> 00:02:26,170
So again, the most common reason for increased alkaline phosphatase ALT and AST is the drug

00:02:26,170 --> 00:02:32,450
as a medication, even Tylenol, pain medication will do that.

00:02:32,450 --> 00:02:37,650
So if you're not at 80 medications whatsoever, the only change you made is SEACT that I would

00:02:37,650 --> 00:02:42,570
say, well, I would definitely go off SEACT and see if it decreases.

00:02:42,570 --> 00:02:48,450
If you, let's say, if it has nothing to do with cancer, it has something to do with irritation

00:02:48,450 --> 00:02:52,730
of the liver because something you're taking, and let's say it was SEACT and you went off

00:02:52,730 --> 00:02:56,730
of it, these numbers should come back to normal relatively quickly.

00:02:56,730 --> 00:03:01,210
Or if it was Tylenol, all I'm taking Tylenol every day, well, if you were able to get off

00:03:01,250 --> 00:03:04,370
of that, these numbers should go down.

00:03:04,370 --> 00:03:13,610
So I would investigate anything you're taking could be, it's very common that Tylenol does

00:03:13,610 --> 00:03:14,610
this.

00:03:14,610 --> 00:03:20,210
So if you're taking something like that or other pain medication or ad bill, but definitely,

00:03:20,210 --> 00:03:24,850
if you're not taking any of those things, I would go off the SEACT and then wait a few

00:03:24,850 --> 00:03:29,490
weeks and see if the numbers stabilize or start to decrease.

00:03:29,490 --> 00:03:37,490
This elevated ALT, AST and Oakland Foss, not taking Tylenol or any other painkillers,

00:03:37,490 --> 00:03:45,090
that I would definitely suspect SEACT, I would, you know, if a person, there wasn't taking

00:03:45,090 --> 00:03:51,690
anything and they had a diagnosis of cancer and they had a rapid increase in those three

00:03:51,690 --> 00:03:57,810
liver markers, you do, I would agree with the oncologist, you'd suspect metastasis to

00:03:57,810 --> 00:03:59,290
the liver.

00:03:59,290 --> 00:04:09,050
If you, or if you had no metastasis to the liver, you'd suspect, you know, an increase activity

